<http://data.silknow.org/object/f161db5b-5bbb-3dc3-8c87-160bc99c7088>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Description: Woven silk and metal thread bordered with woven silk, backed with printed plain weave cotton and faced with printed cotton.\nThe central panel is divided into a small-scale pattern of compartments; in the bottom row there are four almost circular dark blue ground medallions with 3 small lozenges in between.  In the row above there are 3 slightly larger dark blue ground medallions which are more star-like; there are larger lozenges in between.  The rest of the ground is packed with small hexagons with a gold ground and a white flowerhead. All the motifs contain small red details. The dark blue ground medallions each contain a central gold star surrounded by a circular band with red dots and 8 small flowers.\nMetal Thread: gilt strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core.\nBorder: later in date and probably not Persian: dark red satin ground with a large peacock in blue, green, light yellow and purple which has faded to white. A stem with small flowers seems to form a lattice around the birds and there is a green rosette where the stems cross.\nBacking: pieced; white ground printed with a tiny purple flowerhead.\nFacing: bias cut; stripes; white and light brown stripes contain a meandering stem; red and blue stripes contain a small, isolated floral sprig."@en , "woven silk, 1800s, Persian; Birds"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/a0d96788-66c6-3465-9099-bb3df9dfe73b> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/dbd37706-1786-30a5-86ff-271c995de014> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/aaaf526c-58b0-3207-b534-6556bfdf1d62> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "woven silk, 1800s, Persian; Birds"@en , "Description: Woven silk and metal thread bordered with woven silk, backed with printed plain weave cotton and faced with printed cotton.\nThe central panel is divided into a small-scale pattern of compartments; in the bottom row there are four almost circular dark blue ground medallions with 3 small lozenges in between.  In the row above there are 3 slightly larger dark blue ground medallions which are more star-like; there are larger lozenges in between.  The rest of the ground is packed with small hexagons with a gold ground and a white flowerhead. All the motifs contain small red details. The dark blue ground medallions each contain a central gold star surrounded by a circular band with red dots and 8 small flowers.\nMetal Thread: gilt strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core.\nBorder: later in date and probably not Persian: dark red satin ground with a large peacock in blue, green, light yellow and purple which has faded to white. A stem with small flowers seems to form a lattice around the birds and there is a green rosette where the stems cross.\nBacking: pieced; white ground printed with a tiny purple flowerhead.\nFacing: bias cut; stripes; white and light brown stripes contain a meandering stem; red and blue stripes contain a small, isolated floral sprig."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/f161db5b-5bbb-3dc3-8c87-160bc99c7088/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/f161db5b-5bbb-3dc3-8c87-160bc99c7088/dimension/1> ;
